Pyro patch 0035: Trusted Types hooks for eval and Function.

The C-API global used JSGlobalObject's codeForEval and canCompileStrings, so an embedder could
not apply Trusted Types to string compilation. JSGlobalContextSetCompileStringsCallbacks
(API/JSForkPrivate.h) gives JSAPIGlobalObject per-global callbacks for both:
codeForEval turns a TrustedScript passed to eval into its code, canCompileStrings runs the
default policy and the CSP check (and may throw). JSGlobalContextSetTrustedTypesEnforcement sets
the global's require-trusted-types-for state, which decides whether canCompileStrings is asked.

